# Staged Uranium cries land beside the ~1161 TRACKED vanilla cry wavs. This
# used to be an explicit per-species list, and it decayed exactly as its own
# note predicted: CH05 staged GROZARD/TERLARD and the BAASHAUN family, and
# their five wavs sat untracked-and-unignored — ROM-derived audio one
# `git add -A` away from being committed (CLAUDE.md §2). Blanket-ignore the
# directory instead, on the same reasoning as the per-map dirs below: a
# gitignore rule never untracks, so all ~1161 vanilla cries stay tracked and
# committed, and only newly GENERATED (Uranium) wavs are kept out of
# `git status`. The cleaner long-term fix is still to prefix staged cry
# filenames with `uranium_` in species_converter/common.py and ignore that
# glob, which would let this be precise rather than broad.
engine/sound/direct_sound_samples/cries/*.wav
# Full-corpus Map Walker build: the assembler generates a per-map dir under
# data/maps/ and data/layouts/ for every built Uranium map (~190) plus the
# UraniumWalkerStub/ dummy for dropped stock map data. Blanket-ignore all per-map
# dirs — the pristine STOCK dirs are already tracked, so git keeps them; this only
# keeps the generated (Uranium + stub) dirs out of `git status` so ROM-derived
# binaries are never accidentally committed (CLAUDE.md §2).
engine/data/maps/*/
engine/data/layouts/*/
